        "id": "price-order",
        "at": [
          8,
          10
        ],
        "title": "The price board",
        "text": "APPLES 4P in chalk, three days old. A slate underneath lists today’s prices in pencil, crossed out and rewritten twice. A note: TESSA — CAN YOUR LODGER’S SLATE DO THIS? I NEVER KNOW WHAT CHANGED. — T. VASKO"
      },
      {
        "id": "produce",
        "at": [
          4,
          5
        ],
        "title": "The produce stand",
        "text": "Apples, oranges, lemons, cabbages, carrots, plums. Each crate has a tag that says which hill farm it came from, and one that just says ORCHARD in a different hand."
      },
      {
        "id": "jars",
        "at": [
          9,
          10
        ],
        "title": "Jars and tins",
        "text": "Preserves, honey, tea and spices, labelled in neat capitals. Someone has turned every label to face the front."
      },
      {
        "id": "scale",
        "at": [
          8,
          7
        ],
        "title": "The beam scale",
        "text": "Brass, polished where hands rest on it. A single apple sits in the pan as if waiting to be weighed."
      },
      {
        "id": "barrow",
        "at": [
          3,
          2
        ],
        "title": "Teo's barrow",
        "text": "Brought in off the street for the day. T. VASKO · FRUIT & VEG on the board, and under the new paint, older letters showing through: VASKO & CO."
      },
      {
        "id": "bins",
        "at": [
          2,
          10
        ],
        "title": "The bins",
        "text": "Rice, lentils, beans, oats, sugar, coffee. The coffee bin is nearly empty and smells wonderful. Chalked on its lid: ASK TESSA, NOT ME. — T.V."
      },
      {
        "id": "flowers",
        "at": [
          1,
          2
        ],
        "title": "The flower buckets",
        "text": "Tulips, sunflowers, sweet peas. A paper tag tied to the sunflowers: KEEP SIX BACK FOR MIRA."
      }
